FIBEMATE PQC-KEM Native Addon (packages/pqc-kem)
================================================

The C sources under packages/pqc-kem/native/ are vendored from the reference
implementation of the pq-crystals/kyber project:

  Source:            https://github.com/pq-crystals/kyber (ref/ implementation)
  Upstream license:  CC0-1.0 OR Apache-2.0 (dual-licensed, the licensee may choose)
  Used here under:   Apache-2.0, matching packages/pqc-kem/package.json
  Vendored:          2026-07-22, in FIBEMATE commit 59a00bd

The upstream snapshot cannot be pinned to a single commit: 14 of the 25 files are
byte-identical to pq-crystals/kyber da52c4d (2026-07-28), and a fifteenth
(verify.c) is byte-identical to 4768bd37 (2025-02-16). The vendored tree therefore
sits between those revisions.

Files reproduced from upstream without functional change
(an SPDX header is the only addition):
  cbd.c cbd.h fips202.c fips202.h indcpa.h kem.h ntt.c ntt.h poly.h
  reduce.c reduce.h symmetric-shake.c symmetric.h verify.c verify.h

Files derived from upstream and modified by FIBEMATE:
  indcpa.c      added a FIPS 203 domain-separator comment
  kem.c         FIPS 203 decapsulation key layout, dk = dkPKE || ek || H(ek) || z
  params.h      rewritten parameter header, including the KYBER_NAMESPACE macro
  poly.c        upstream compile-time guard relaxed to a comment
  polyvec.c     upstream compile-time guard relaxed to a comment
  polyvec.h     removed the upstream KYBER_NAMESPACE rename block
  randombytes.c replaced with /dev/urandom and BCryptGenRandom
  randombytes.h kept for the derandomised API

Original FIBEMATE code, not derived from upstream:
  mlkem_wrap.c  Node-API addon glue
  params_768.h  ML-KEM-768 parameter header

fips202.c and fips202.h carry public-domain Keccak code by Ronny Van Keer and the
"TweetFips202" implementation by Gilles Van Assche, Daniel J. Bernstein and Peter
Schwabe. The attribution comment at the top of fips202.c is retained verbatim.

The repository as a whole is distributed under GPL-3.0 (see LICENSE). This package
is distributed under Apache-2.0 as declared in packages/pqc-kem/package.json;
Apache-2.0 is compatible with GPL-3.0, so the combined work can be distributed
under GPL-3.0 as well.
